(3880699, 544763, 60862, '<td valign="top">Wow, Bobbie!  What a cool image.  Congrats on top 4 and a new personal best! :)</td>', 'Wow, Bobbie!  What a cool image.  Congrats on top 4 and a new personal best! :)', '2007-07-08 03:57:54.000000', NULL, 0),
(3880783, 544543, 62095, '<td valign="top">Neat idea.  For me, to make the circuit board part work, you would need to mould it more in 3D, because at the moment the board does not match the curvature of the arm, and so it is difficult to believe in.  The part where I find this most evident is the bottom right of the circuit board, where the curve should be fairly large.  Perhaps if you do not have the tools to mold the board in that way, then you could "cover" the board with some skin in the areas where it should be folded.  (So what I mean there is to not have the skin uniformly square around the board, but use more of a "cloud".)<br/> <br/>I may also have gone for more of a "claw" like position with the hand, fingers closer together.</td>', 'Neat idea.  For me, to make the circuit board part work, you would need to mould it more in 3D, because at the moment the board does not match the curvature of the arm, and so it is difficult to believe in.  The part where I find this most evident is the bottom right of the circuit board, where the curve should be fairly large.  Perhaps if you do not have the tools to mold the board in that way, then you could "cover" the board with some skin in the areas where it should be folded.  (So what I mean there is to not have the skin uniformly square around the board, but use more of a "cloud".) I may also have gone for more of a "claw" like position with the hand, fingers closer together.', '2007-07-08 05:18:23.000000', NULL, 0),
(3880965, 544402, 3032, '<td valign="top">Told you it would ribbon.</td>', 'Told you it would ribbon.', '2007-07-08 08:01:59.000000', NULL, 0),
